  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "5951196",
      "title": "Isolated vs Non-Isolated Tests",
      "lectureOrder": 732,
      "videoOrder": 673,
      "sourceHash": "a2966190fe4a52d41c802431e40a260953c5e0c2df903c98373bb4ef007ba93d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.71,
          "end": 3.24,
          "en": "-: This is our example app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.24,
          "end": 5.25,
          "en": "And as you can see, we get a user component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.25,
          "end": 7.184,
          "en": "and a user service, and both are connected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.184,
          "end": 10.003,
          "en": "because we inject the user service in the user component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.003,
          "end": 13.11,
          "en": "Now, let's say we have a reverse pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.11,
          "end": 14.717,
          "en": "which reverses any string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.717,
          "end": 18.54,
          "en": "That pipe can be tested, isolated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.54,
          "end": 20.88,
          "en": "We do have this Angular 2 package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.88,
          "end": 22.26,
          "en": "or these Angular 2 utilities.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.26,
          "end": 26.309,
          "en": "You saw test bed, async, tick, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.309,
          "end": 29.37,
          "en": "There are a couple of utilities in this package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.37,
          "end": 31.613,
          "en": "and actually you already saw most of them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.613,
          "end": 34.26,
          "en": "The others can be seen in the reference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.26,
          "end": 36.33,
          "en": "I'll link in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.33,
          "end": 39.78,
          "en": "But anyways, a pipe can be tested",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.78,
          "end": 42.36,
          "en": "totally independent of Angular 2.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.36,
          "end": 43.41,
          "en": "Why?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 43.41,
          "end": 45.06,
          "en": "Because how does a pipe work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 45.06,
          "end": 49.47,
          "en": "It has this transform function where you pass a string in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 49.47,
          "end": 51.75,
          "en": "and get a string out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 51.75,
          "end": 55.5,
          "en": "No need to involve Angular 2 for such a basic pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 55.5,
          "end": 57.48,
          "en": "You might have other tasks in your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 57.48,
          "end": 58.59,
          "en": "where the same is true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 58.59,
          "end": 61.14,
          "en": "If you get a service and in the service you get a method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 61.14,
          "end": 63.26,
          "en": "which only transforms some data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 63.26,
          "end": 66.18,
          "en": "or let's say, doubles the number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 66.18,
          "end": 68.25,
          "en": "Well then you can test it isolated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 68.25,
          "end": 70.77,
          "en": "You don't need the Angular 2 testing package for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 70.77,
          "end": 72.6,
          "en": "You can write a normal unit test.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 72.6,
          "end": 73.646,
          "en": "And this is what I'll show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 73.646,
          "end": 76.056,
          "en": "at the example of a reverse pipe now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 76.056,
          "end": 79.32,
          "en": "I will create the pipe in the shared folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 79.32,
          "end": 81.12,
          "en": "and I'll create it manually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 81.12,
          "end": 85.47,
          "en": "I'll name it reverse.pipe.ts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 85.47,
          "end": 88.23,
          "en": "And in there we of course export a class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 88.23,
          "end": 90.43299999999999,
          "en": "which is named ReversePipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 93.78,
          "end": 98.03999999999999,
          "en": "And on this class, we attach the pipe decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 98.03999999999999,
          "end": 101.52000000000001,
          "en": "as you learned it to be imported from @angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 101.52000000000001,
          "end": 103.17,
          "en": "And there I pass an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 103.17,
          "end": 105.71000000000001,
          "en": "where I give it a name of reverse.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 105.71000000000001,
          "end": 108,
          "en": "Well, and inside of this class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 108,
          "end": 111.783,
          "en": "I therefore need to have the transform function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 113.52000000000001,
          "end": 116.876,
          "en": "And this transform function expects to get a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 116.876,
          "end": 119.693,
          "en": "or devalue, let's say, which is a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 119.693,
          "end": 124.693,
          "en": "and possibly some params, though I won't pass some here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 125.4,
          "end": 128.463,
          "en": "Well, and then I can simply return the value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 129.69,
          "end": 130.713,
          "en": "split it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 133.02,
          "end": 137.37,
          "en": "by well, nothing, so that each character is separated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 137.37,
          "end": 139.695,
          "en": "So split it by each character, basically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 139.695,
          "end": 141.54,
          "en": "Call reverse on that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 141.54,
          "end": 143.79,
          "en": "That's a normal function available on an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 143.79,
          "end": 145.703,
          "en": "And a string is just an array of characters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 145.703,
          "end": 147.835,
          "en": "And then join them again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 147.835,
          "end": 151.006,
          "en": "with nothing in between joining them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 151.006,
          "end": 153.09,
          "en": "so that each character is attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 153.09,
          "end": 154.23,
          "en": "to the character before it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 154.23,
          "end": 156.99,
          "en": "without a white space in between or something like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 156.99,
          "end": 159.085,
          "en": "That is what my reverse pipe does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 159.085,
          "end": 161.88,
          "en": "Well, and now for testing this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 161.88,
          "end": 163.86,
          "en": "I can really write my own",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 163.86,
          "end": 168.86,
          "en": "reverse pipe spec.ts file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 170.7,
          "end": 173.787,
          "en": "Now if we have a look at the user component spec file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 173.787,
          "end": 176.52,
          "en": "how does a spec file look like?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 176.52,
          "end": 179.34,
          "en": "Well, if I copy it, which is a bit overkill.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 179.34,
          "end": 181.284,
          "en": "Whoops, not here. Here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 181.284,
          "end": 185.16,
          "en": "I of course want to get rid of all the it statements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 185.16,
          "end": 186.371,
          "en": "except for one, maybe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 186.371,
          "end": 188.28,
          "en": "Get rid of all these imports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 188.28,
          "end": 191.64,
          "en": "and I can also get rid of the Angular 2 testing utilities",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 191.64,
          "end": 192.75,
          "en": "because I don't need them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 192.75,
          "end": 195,
          "en": "I also don't need them before each.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 195,
          "end": 197.256,
          "en": "There is no setup to be run before each pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 197.256,
          "end": 200.28,
          "en": "All I wanna do here, for example, is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 200.28,
          "end": 203.46,
          "en": "I want to create my reverse pipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 203.46,
          "end": 205.74,
          "en": "which is a new reverse pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 205.74,
          "end": 207.81,
          "en": "And that is why it's called isolated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 207.81,
          "end": 209.61,
          "en": "It doesn't depend on any other piece",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 209.61,
          "end": 210.96,
          "en": "in my Angular 2 application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 210.96,
          "end": 213.27,
          "en": "It doesn't even depend on Angular 2.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 213.27,
          "end": 214.5,
          "en": "And all I want do is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 214.5,
          "end": 217.656,
          "en": "I want to expect reverse pipe transform.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 217.656,
          "end": 221.52,
          "en": "If I pass, let's say, \"Hello\" in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 221.52,
          "end": 225.87,
          "en": "to equal well, and then this should be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 225.87,
          "end": 228.543,
          "en": "O L L E H.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 229.65,
          "end": 230.52,
          "en": "That is all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 230.52,
          "end": 234.93,
          "en": "And if I save this, we should now have 11 successful tests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 234.93,
          "end": 238.82999999999998,
          "en": "because this clearly should succeed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 238.82999999999998,
          "end": 241.86,
          "en": "And we do see 11 successful tests indeed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 241.86,
          "end": 243.66,
          "en": "after rerunning each test,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 243.66,
          "end": 246.89,
          "en": "or if you still had it running after saving.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 246.89,
          "end": 249.09,
          "en": "This is an isolated test.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 249.09,
          "end": 251.49,
          "en": "Of course you could have some pipe which depends",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 251.49,
          "end": 253.148,
          "en": "on Angular 2 or something like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 253.148,
          "end": 256.08,
          "en": "And it really comes down to this question.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 256.08,
          "end": 258.18,
          "en": "Does the thing you want to test depend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 258.18,
          "end": 260.82,
          "en": "on Angular 2 or other pieces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 260.82,
          "end": 262.45,
          "en": "of your Angular 2 application?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 262.45,
          "end": 265.92,
          "en": "If yes, well then you get these testing utilities",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 265.92,
          "end": 268.59,
          "en": "like test bed, which allows you to create components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 268.59,
          "end": 271.62,
          "en": "access the injector, set up the module for testing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 271.62,
          "end": 272.46,
          "en": "and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 272.46,
          "end": 274.53,
          "en": "You get async, fakeAsync, and tick,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 274.53,
          "end": 278.55,
          "en": "to, well, handle asynchronous tasks and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 278.55,
          "end": 280.765,
          "en": "In the lecture, at the end of this module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 280.765,
          "end": 284.01,
          "en": "you will learn more about other resources,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 284.01,
          "end": 285.51,
          "en": "about other tests you could write,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 285.51,
          "end": 287.197,
          "en": "other things you can test.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 287.197,
          "end": 290.19,
          "en": "If you don't have that, if you don't have a dependency",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 290.19,
          "end": 291.959,
          "en": "on Angular 2 or other pieces in the app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 291.959,
          "end": 296.348,
          "en": "well then, an isolated test like this might be all you need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 296.348,
          "end": 300.54,
          "en": "And with that, we had a good introduction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 300.54,
          "end": 302.61,
          "en": "to how testing here works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 302.61,
          "end": 306.33,
          "en": "how we can use the Angular 2 testing package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 306.33,
          "end": 308.94,
          "en": "The features it offers us to write our tests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 308.94,
          "end": 310.32,
          "en": "to use services.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 310.32,
          "end": 312.467,
          "en": "And as I already said at the beginning,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 312.467,
          "end": 315.034,
          "en": "I could continue for a couple of hours here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 315.034,
          "end": 317.28,
          "en": "but this is not what this course is about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 317.28,
          "end": 319.765,
          "en": "and not what I want to make this course about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 319.765,
          "end": 321.559,
          "en": "It is a good introduction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 321.559,
          "end": 324.78,
          "en": "With that, you should be able to dive really deeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 324.78,
          "end": 327.73,
          "en": "into it with the article in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 327.73,
          "end": 330.109,
          "en": "You should be able to use your general",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 330.109,
          "end": 332.545,
          "en": "unit testing knowledge you already have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 332.545,
          "end": 335.76,
          "en": "to take advantage of these tools Angular 2 offers you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 335.76,
          "end": 338.293,
          "en": "to create components to access them and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 338.293,
          "end": 340.40999999999997,
          "en": "And with that, that is all I can do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 340.40999999999997,
          "end": 342.63,
          "en": "I can encourage you to dive deeper into it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 342.63,
          "end": 345.398,
          "en": "And I hope this introduction was at least helpful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 345.398,
          "end": 348.231,
          "en": "to understand how you might decide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 348.231,
          "end": 351.33,
          "en": "when to test the connection of Angular 2",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 351.33,
          "end": 353.43,
          "en": "and your component or whatever",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 353.43,
          "end": 354.879,
          "en": "and when to test it isolated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 354.879,
          "end": 357.552,
          "en": "Why unit tests are helpful in the first place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 357.552,
